  "description": "A rare opportunity to register your interest in accommodation within the historic Knocktopher Abbey estate, Co. Kilkenny.\n \n \nA limited number of self-contained residential units within Knocktopher House are to become available in Summer 2026.\n \nThe accommodation is comprised of: \n\n9 x 1 bedroom self contained apartments completely with kitchen and bathroom. Price ranging from €1,600 for the two larger units to €1,250 for the smallest at loft level. \n\nThese lettings are intended for individuals seeking unique accommodation in a peaceful countryside setting\n \nInterested parties are invited to submit their details and accommodation requirements, and the appointed agent will make contact as units become available.\n \n \nProperty Features\n \n- Landmark Victorian Gothic abbey estate of exceptional character and heritage\n- Rare opportunity to reside within one of County Kilkenny’s most distinctive historic properties\n- Self-contained accommodation within converted courtyard, coach house, and stable buildings\n- Unique architectural features and period surroundings\n- Mature landscaped grounds with woodland walks and countryside views\n- Extensive outdoor space and natural surroundings\n- Ample on-site parking\n- Low-density residential environment with strong privacy and tranquillity\n \nLocation & Accessibility\n \n- Located in the heart of South Kilkenny near the village of Knocktopher\n- Excellent access to the M9 motorway via nearby Junction 10\n- Approx. 20 minutes to Kilkenny City\n- Approx. 30 minutes to Waterford City\n- Approx. 90 minutes to Dublin via motorway connection\n- Convenient access to the wider South East region including Carlow, Wexford, and Tipperary\n- Well positioned rs travelling between Kilkenny and Waterford\n- Thomastown railway station approximately 10 minutes away with rail connections on the Dublin–Waterford line",
